<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Caucasus</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Alania</h1><p class="st-meta">800 CE – 1239 CE (approx.) · capital Maghas</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The medieval Christian kingdom of the Alans in the North Caucasus, a Byzantine ally and Georgian partner until the Mongols destroyed it in 1239.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/alans">Alans</a> who stayed in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-caucasus">North Caucasus</a> after the Hunnic invasions came under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/khazar-khaganate">Khazar Khaganate</a>. As <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate">Khazar</a> power declined in the 10th century, Alanian rulers formed a kingdom along the upper Kuban and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/terek-river">Terek</a> rivers, and around 916 they accepted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> from a Byzantine mission sent by Patriarch <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicholas-i-mystikos">Nicholas Mystikos</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Kings ruled a land of fortified towns and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hill-fort">hill forts</a>, controlling the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darial-pass">Darial Pass</a> and trade with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> and the steppe. The Alanian church had its own metropolitan, and stone churches survive in the Zelenchuk valley. Royal marriages linked the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/alans">Alans</a> to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-georgia">Kingdom of Georgia</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/byzantium">Byzantium</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamar-of-georgia">Queen Tamar's</a> husband <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david-soslan">David Soslan</a> was an Alanian prince.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> defeated the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/alans">Alans</a> in 1222, and in 1239 they stormed the capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalinga-magha">Maghas</a>. Survivors withdrew into the mountains, where their descendants became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ossetians">Ossetians</a>. Others fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a> and Mongol service in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, and the name of Alania survives in the official title of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-ossetia-alania">North Ossetia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-alania.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Alania" width="320" height="249"><figcaption>Image: Constantine Plakidas · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Caucasus_1060_map_en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>800 CE – 1239 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Maghas</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Durgulel the Great</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Alanic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Alania, Kingdom of the Alans</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1020&amp;focus=kingdom-of-alania" aria-label="Kingdom of Alania on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5625 198 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Alania lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6131 811h0M7559 780h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5945 454h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5945 454h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Russia. <a href="/atlas?year=1020&amp;focus=kingdom-of-alania">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
